{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/439562-real-world-inspirations","id":439562,"title":"Real-World Inspirations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-13T00:35:37-07:00","id":439562,"title":"Real-World Inspirations","content":"Every once in a while I run across something that instantly makes me think &quot;hey, that would be really cool to include in a game!&quot; For instance, while driving through San Francisco to a weekly writing group I always pass this little bar called the Owl Tree, which makes me think of <i>The Strix Chronicle</i> every time. The front of the place is covered with this great mosaic, part of which is pictured here:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-0vP51zE6p6w/TYyltDOQ8xI/AAAAAAAADhM/CTLY67dY7Ug/s1600/owl-9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I find the image is even more striking at night, but it's really cool either way. Inside, the place is decorated all in reds, blacks, and dark mahogany, and with just a little tweaking it could make a perfect setting for clandestine meetings between genteel monsters.<br /> <br /> Has anybody else run across something similarly inspiring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 03-13-2015, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:40:09-07:00","id":440617,"title":"","content":"I also discovered the Owl Tree while looking around San Francisco locations online for a <b>Requiem</b> game. (The PCs ended up stealing a stuffed owl from it because they needed owl feathers for a Strix-repelling ritual in a hurry.)<br /> <br /> Here in Edinburgh, we're at the forefront of developing <a href=\"http://www.medicaldaily.com/scientists-create-artificial-blood-can-be-produced-industrial-scale-limitless-supply-blood-276830\" target=\"_blank\">synthetic blood</a>. I figure that has to be worth the attention of local vampires...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:12:50-07:00","id":440712,"title":"","content":"Once found this tag while I was out canvassing for a charity, back in the bad old days when I canvassed for a charity. I'm pretty sure this is some sort of Cacophony tag (wrong initials, though):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/gatz9l7kr0r51ey/Prince%20of%20Van%20City.jpg?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/gatz9l7kr0r51ey/Prince%20of%20Van%20City.jpg?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/gatz9l7kr0r51ey/Prince%20of%20Van%20City.jpg?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.dropbox.com/s/gatz9l7kr0r51ey/Prince%20of%20Van%20City.jpg?dl=0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T19:05:40-07:00","id":440774,"title":"","content":"I used to work a lot on a pier in Miami.<br /> <br /> One day there was this old lady there in a wheelchair. Nothing out of the ordinary, but she started talking to me and told me that she was there when they made the beaches. She told me that they, presumably the army corps of engineers, had dozens if not hundreds of horses dragging out sand to form a bed that would catch more and sand develop into a beach. They didn't take the horses away, though. She said they just killed them there when they were done, and the water was full of blood.<br /> <br /> I've looked it up, and it doesn't seem to be accurate, but I've used it as a plot point in my stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:56:51-07:00","id":440926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/439562-real-world-inspirations?p=440712#post440712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once found this tag while I was out canvassing for a charity, back in the bad old days when I canvassed for a charity. I'm pretty sure this is some sort of Cacophony tag (wrong initials, though):<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/gatz9l7kr0r51ey/Prince%20of%20Van%20City.jpg?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/gatz9l7kr0...0City.jpg?dl=0</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me; I have a friend who has the unusual hobby of collecting stickers (mostly packing labels) that people have used to put up street art here in the Bay Area. He's got a website <a href=\"http://www.stickerstealer.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> where he's posted part of his collection, if anybody's curious. I can easily imagine using an ersatz version of him in a game, since he seems like exactly the sort of person that might notice secret messages encoded in graffiti.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 03-14-2015, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T00:12:24-07:00","id":441044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/439562-real-world-inspirations?p=440774#post440774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to work a lot on a pier in Miami.<br /> <br /> One day there was this old lady there in a wheelchair. Nothing out of the ordinary, but she started talking to me and told me that she was there when they made the beaches. She told me that they, presumably the army corps of engineers, had dozens if not hundreds of horses dragging out sand to form a bed that would catch more and sand develop into a beach. They didn't take the horses away, though. She said they just killed them there when they were done, and the water was full of blood.<br /> <br /> I've looked it up, and it doesn't seem to be accurate, but I've used it as a plot point in my stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>The blood and carcasses could have been used to draw reef building marine life in the water and accelerate the growth of sandy grasses and shrubs on the sand to stymie erosion. Needlessly cruel perhaps but the Army Corps of Engineers aren't in the business of sheltering animals and the U. S. government has never been known for being frugal with other people's money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 03-14-2015, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:32:35-07:00","id":441454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/439562-real-world-inspirations?p=441044#post441044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The blood and carcasses could have been used to draw reef building marine life in the water and accelerate the growth of sandy grasses and shrubs on the sand to stymie erosion. Needlessly cruel perhaps but the Army Corps of Engineers aren't in the business of sheltering animals and the U. S. government has never been known for being frugal with other people's money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool and weird. I have to say as horrible as it must have been it does add some angles to it. And I'd hate to think the old woman was just picking me out to lie to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T12:02:19-07:00","id":441679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/439562-real-world-inspirations?p=441044#post441044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The blood and carcasses could have been used to draw reef building marine life in the water and accelerate the growth of sandy grasses and shrubs on the sand to stymie erosion. Needlessly cruel perhaps but the Army Corps of Engineers aren't in the business of sheltering animals and the U. S. government has never been known for being frugal with other people's money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of reminds me of that vampire machine thing from <i>Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead</i> that depends on a unique type of coral to function...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T14:38:26-07:00","id":446544,"title":"","content":"Just found out that there's a social club (In the vein of a historical 'gentleman's club') with private, invite-only membership, attached to a nightclub in my city that is collectively called <i>Elysium</i>. It describes the aesthetic, on the very nice posters posted around campus which even deliberately invoke vampire imagery, as both &quot;Gothic and New Wave&quot;. That was quite the smack in the face noticing it. There is something deeply and disturbingly funny about the Prince of the city (or at least the person in charge of Elysium) flirting rather openly at the edge of the Masquerade to the point that it would be as obvious as a huge sign say &quot;VAMPIRES HANG OUT HERE&quot; to anyone who knows much of anything about the supernatural community at large in the WoD.<br /> <br /> Am I going to abuse the hell out of this for a good story? Absolutely- it's far too good to pass up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}